note A graph node's header has more-above and more-below icon buttons that show ten more lines of its file above or below its own lines, the way the document's context buttons do, with the node's own lines highlighted; 'no context' cuts it back to its own lines. The reader reaches for it to see what surrounds a node's lines without leaving the graph. A node longer than the preview also has 'more'/'less', which switches between a preview of its first lines and its full text. Widening or narrowing pins the node where it is, so the change does not shuffle the layout.

